Your task: ensure every HLR is covered by a MODULE.
{% include "shared/tool_reminder.j2" %} {% include "shared/node_id_format.j2" %}
{% include "shared/multi_write_tip.j2" %}

Steps:
1. graph_read — list all HLR nodes.
2. graph_read — list all existing MODULE nodes.
3. For each uncovered HLR, add it to the most relevant MODULE:
   graph_add_traces(node_id=<module_id>, trace_to=["<hlr_id>"])
   add_traces APPENDS the HLR to the existing list — it never replaces other entries.
4. Only create a NEW MODULE if none exist yet:
   graph_add_node(node_type=MODULE, parent_id=<ARCHITECTURE node ID>, trace_to=[<HLR IDs>], title='3–5 words').

Simplest-solution principle: a single MODULE covering all HLRs is preferred.
